      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nIn a headless SFCC architecture the storefront presentation layer runs independently of the Salesforce Commerce Cloud backend. The SFCC platform is responsible exclusively for:\n\n* Business logic (pricing, promotions, tax, inventory)\n* Order management and checkout orchestration\n* Catalog management via Business Manager\n* Cartridge-based custom logic exposed through SCAPI / OCAPI\n\n**Scope of this document:** This page covers the SFCC-side build and deployment only — cartridge packaging, WebDAV upload, code version activation, Business Manager configuration, and data import/export. Frontend (Next.js / PWA Kit) deployment is documented separately — see PWA CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions).\n\n---\n\nSFCC deployment activities\n--------------------------\n\n1. **Developer commit:** SFCC cartridge code, metadata, jobs, services, hooks, and site-specific configuration changes are committed to the agreed source repository.\n2. **CI build:** The pipeline validates the cartridge structure, runs linting/unit checks, installs dependencies, and produces a deployable cartridge bundle.\n3. **Install vendor cartridges:**`npm run vendor:install` copies third-party cartridges from `vendor/` into `cartridges/` before packaging.\n4. **Package cartridges:** All cartridges in `cartridges/` are zipped in the required cartridge path order for the target SFCC instance.\n5. **Deploy to sandbox or development:** The package is uploaded to the SFCC instance using WebDAV or the approved deployment automation.\n6. **Activate code version:** A new code version is created or updated in Business Manager, then activated for validation.\n7. **Import configuration and data:** Required site preferences, custom objects, metadata, jobs, services, promotions, catalog, inventory, price book, and content changes are imported as applicable.\n8. **Rebuild search index:** After any data import the `RebuildALLSearchIndex` job is triggered automatically to ensure product search reflects the latest catalog state across all sites.\n9. **Validate SFCC functionality:** QA confirms cartridge behavior, Business Manager configuration, API responses, checkout flows, payment integrations, tax, shipping, promotions, and order export behavior.\n10. **Promote through environments:** The same validated package and configuration set moves through QA, Staging, and Production following approval gates.\n11. **Production release:** The production code version is activated, final imports are completed, smoke tests are run, and rollback readiness is confirmed.\n\n---\n\nEnvironment progression\n-----------------------\n\n| Stage | SFCC ENV | Purpose | Primary outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Local | Sandboxes | Developer local feature validation | Specific feature and story |\n| Development | BKZK-002 | Initial deployment and technical verification | Confirm package integrity and baseline functionality |\n| TEST | BKZK-005 | Initial deployment and technical verification | Confirm package integrity and baseline functionality |\n| SIT | BKZK-003 | Functional and regression validation | Integration readiness |\n| UAT | DEV-AP01 | Functional and regression validation | Verify business behavior and integration readiness |\n| Staging | STG-AP01 | Pre-production validation in a production-like setup | Support final business and release checks |\n| Production | PROD-AP01 | Live customer-facing deployment | Activate the approved backend code version |\n\n---\n\nRepository and cartridge structure\n----------------------------------\n\nnonezimmermann-sfcc/\n├── cartridges/\n│ ├── int\\_custom\\_zim\\_global/ # Zimmermann — global integrations & job steps\n│ ├── plugin\\_zim\\_scapi/ # Zimmermann — SCAPI / OCAPI hook overrides\n│ ├── int\\_globale/ # Global-e (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ ├── int\\_globale\\_headless/ # Global-e headless (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ ├── int\\_avatax\\_svcclient/ # Avalara AvaTax service client (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ ├── int\\_avatax\\_sfra/ # Avalara AvaTax SFRA (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n│ └── bm\\_avatax/ # Avalara AvaTax BM extension (generated by vendor:install — do not edit)\n├── vendor/ # Third-party packages — source of truth (protected)\n│ ├── VENDORS.md # Upgrade runbook and package inventory\n│ ├── globale-v24.5.0/ # Full Global-e package + vendor.config.json\n│ └── avatax-v24.1.0/ # Full Avalara AvaTax package + vendor.config.json\n├── scripts/\n│ └── vendor-install.js # Reads vendor.config.json files, copies cartridges\n├── data/\n│ ├── core/ # Baseline data — imported to all envs\n│ └── sample/ # Dev/demo data — imported manually\n├── docs/ # Project documentation\n├── .github/\n│ ├── CODEOWNERS # vendor/ protected by @mani060689\n│ └── workflows/ # CI/CD pipeline definitions\n├── .env.example # Environment variable template\n├── package.json # Scripts, workspace config, Jest config\n└── build/ # Generated — gitignored\n> **Note:** Vendor cartridges under `cartridges/` are gitignored and generated at build time by `npm run vendor:install`. Never edit them directly — make changes in `vendor/` instead.\n>\n> **Note:** The `vendor/` folder requires approval from @mani060689 before any PR can be merged.\n\n### Adding or upgrading a vendor cartridge\n\n1. Download the new version zip from the vendor source.\n2. Create `vendor/<package>-v<version>/` and extract the zip into it.\n3. Add a `vendor.config.json` (copy from the previous version, update paths and version number).\n4. Delete the old version folder and update `vendor/VENDORS.md`.\n5. Run `npm run vendor:install` to apply changes locally.\n6. Commit `vendor/` changes together with any `data/` and `docs/` additions.\n\n---\n\nData and metadata deployment\n----------------------------\n\nData deployments are handled separately from code. They use SFCC's Site Archive (impex) mechanism and run as a distinct pipeline stage or manual job.\n\nThis data deployment does not apply to production since it is handled via Replication. Each code or data deployment is packaged and versioned and added to GitHub artifacts for promotion to environments.\n\n<https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/whiteboard/265256967>\n\n---\n\nGitHub Actions workflows\n------------------------\n\nThe repository contains five workflow files under `.github/workflows/`. Together they cover every stage of the development lifecycle from pull request through to staging.\n\n### Workflow overview\n\n| File | Name | Trigger | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `ci.yml` | CI | Push to `develop`, `feature/**`, `bugfix/**`, `hotfix/**`, `release/**`; PR to `main` or `develop` | Lint, unit tests (90% coverage threshold), XML schema validation |\n| `pr-check.yml` | PR Check | PR to `develop` or `main` | Quality gate — tests with coverage, posts coverage comment on the PR |\n| `cd-deploy.yml` | CD — Deploy (dev / SIT) | Push to `develop`; manual `workflow_dispatch` | Deploy code and data to Development (BKZK-002) or SIT (BKZK-003) |\n| `cd-test.yml` | CD — Test (scheduled) | Scheduled twice daily at 7am and 7pm AEST; manual `workflow_dispatch` | Full refresh of TEST (BKZK-005) — code, core data, vendor data, search index |\n| `cd-release.yml` | CD — Release (staging + UAT) | **Manual `workflow_dispatch` only** — staging and UAT deployments are always controlled | Deploy code and data to UAT (DEV-AP01) and Staging (STG-AP01) |\n\n---\n\n### ci.yml — Continuous Integration\n\n**Triggers:** Every push to `develop`, `feature/**`, `bugfix/**`, `hotfix/**`, `release/**` branches, and every PR targeting `main` or `develop`.\n\n**Jobs:**\n\n| Job | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| Lint & Unit Tests | Runs `npm run lint` and `npm run test:coverage`. Enforces 90% coverage threshold across branches, functions, lines, and statements. Publishes JUnit test results and uploads coverage report as a GitHub artifact (14-day retention). |\n\n**K